      "name": "Argelys Samuel Oriach",
      "description": "Dominican-born systems architect and performance artist working through writing, voice, movement, and design. Author of This Is Not a Love Story; currently writing a pilot, a play, and his debut hybrid collection, Graduation. He constructs systems and inhabits them. Performance is the governing method of his practice; writing, voice, movement, design, and corporate roles are its forms. Born in the Dominican Republic, Argelys Samuel Oriach was raised by a housekeeper and a facility maintainer, and learned in adulthood that his mother was a writer and his father a musician, though neither pursued their craft. Because of this, he understands creative capacity entirely through the physical infrastructure required to sustain it. A method actor trained in the Alexander Technique, Oriach studies how people look, listen, move, and affect one another. He operates two laboratories: Seven Eighty Three (Lab 783), an independent systems design practice, and Wild Lake Studio, its research laboratory, which guides developing and independent artists. This Is Not a Love Story is a screenplay written in prose form. He is the founder and artistic director of Wild Lake Studio.",
